Aerie-Purpose: Add the backend of the Aerie Guard section of Settings: the message handler on chrome://settings, the pref that hides the count on the Guard icon, and the section's strings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_ui.cc, BUILD.gn, settings_localized_strings_provider.cc), chrome/browser/prefs (browser_prefs.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc, chrome/app/generated_resources.grd
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #103. The handler, the pref helper and the strings are in the overlay:
chrome/browser/ui/webui/aerie_guard_settings (handler, BUILD.gn, the grdp) and
components/aerie_adblock/browser/aerie_guard_prefs.*. SettingsUI adds the handler as a
plain message handler, so it exists on chrome://settings and nowhere else. The pref
aerie.guard.show_blocked_count is a profile pref, on by default. The settings_private
allowlist line lets the page's settings-toggle-button write it; the name is a string
literal there, as for aerie.widevine.enabled, and a test compares it with
aerie_guard::kShowBlockedCount. The strings part sits after the Aerie Guard strings of
adblock/0017 and before the Widevine prompt strings of widevine/0005, so the series
lists this patch after both.

